chart bar dq x=type y=Q2,Q3 unit=% labels title="30+ day delinquency, Q2 vs Q3"

table = Loan type,Balance,Q2,Q3,Change; Personal,$143M,3.4%,4.1%,**+0.7 pts**; Revolving credit,$96M,2.8%,3.0%,+0.2 pts; Auto,$412M,1.9%,2.2%,**+0.3 pts**; Mortgage,$988M,0.6%,0.6%,0.0 pts; **Total**,**$1,639M**,**1.3%**,**1.4%**,**+0.1 pts**

# What changed

- **Personal loans** have the highest delinquency (4.1%) and the largest rise, up 0.7 points in one quarter.
- **Auto** is rising more slowly, up 0.3 points, but matters more in dollars: at $412M it is nearly three times the personal book.
- **Mortgages**, 60.3% of balances, were flat at 0.6%.
- **Revolving credit** edged up 0.2 points to 3.0%.

data bal = type,balance; Mortgage,988; Auto,412; Personal,143; Revolving credit,96

chart hbar bal unit=$M labels title="Balances by loan type ($M)"

# Actions

step Tighten personal loan underwriting for credit scores below 640 | 2026-11-15
step Add early outreach for auto loans at 15 days past due
step Review reserve adequacy | January board meeting
